Description: Port rbgen to Python 3
 rbgen was written for Python 2: it used the removed string module
 functions, the statement forms of exec and raise, and exec to assign
 local variables, which Python 3 does not support inside a function.
 Replace them with str methods, call syntax, and explicit assignments.
 Required to build with --with-python=/usr/bin/python on systems
 without Python 2. Applies on top of rbgen.in.patch.
Forwarded: not-needed, upstream has been inactive since 2003
Last-Update: 2026-11-07

